                <pb facs="0564" n="550" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg550"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/9–1244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Alexander C. Kirk, United States Political Adviser
                        on the Staff of the Supreme Allied Commander, Mediterranean Theater</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caserta</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-12T11:00:00+02:00">September 12,
                            1944—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:54 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>364. My 312, September 7. Colonel Barnes has now reported that on September 9 Von
                    Lanz stated that he would send senior officers immediately to AFHQ if terms are
                    altered from unconditional surrender to surrender. SAC has replied to this
                    message that terms of surrender must remain unconditional surrender and that Von
                    Lanz should be informed that details to implement such surrender will be
                    presented to his representative at AFHQ who must be empowered by Von Lanz to
                    accept or refuse the terms offered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
